import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description="How WhatisAI uses optional visitor analytics.">
  <article class="container section prose" style="max-width:760px">
    <h1>Privacy at WhatisAI</h1>
    <p>Learning progress is saved in your browser. Analytics is optional and separate from your learning records.</p>
    <h2>Optional visitor analytics</h2><p>If you choose “Allow analytics,” PostHog receives page visits, referral domains, device and browser information, reading depth, link destinations, and learning activity events such as starting or finishing a challenge. A random browser identifier stored on this device helps count returning visitors. We do not connect it to your Google account or send your name, email, quiz answers, scores, confidence ratings, goal dates, or progress records. URL query strings and fragments are removed. Session recordings, automatic form capture, advertising, and person profiles are disabled.</p>
    <p>Analytics starts only after your permission. Declining or withdrawing permission stops collection; browser Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control signals also disable it. Use “Analytics preferences” at the bottom of any page to change your choice. Withdrawal clears the analytics identifier on this device and stops future collection; it does not delete events already received by PostHog. The free PostHog plan provides one year of event retention. See <a href="https://posthog.com/privacy">PostHog’s privacy policy</a>.</p>
    <h2>Hosting</h2><p>The site is hosted on GitHub Pages, which receives normal web requests. See <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub’s privacy statement</a>.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
